{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"The first real differential failure is in `SPX_set_keypair_addr`: C writes all four big-endian bytes at offset 20 (offset 10 for SHA-2), while Rust writes only the low two bytes. I’m fixing the translation to preserve the full `uint32_t`, then rerunning this surface across all backends because their offsets differ."}}
