{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"agent_message","text":"The corruption pinpoints unusual C behavior that must be preserved: BLAKE `SPX_gen_message_random` writes the full 32- or 64-byte digest into `R`, even though callers advance by only `SPX_N`. Rust currently writes only `SPX_N`. I’m widening the BLAKE FFI output view and copying the full digest so direct external calls match C byte-for-byte."}}
