{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_136","type":"agent_message","text":"The failure is isolated to FFI alias handling, not the core signing math. The C wrapper signs in place before its final `memmove`, so the Rust wrapper must preserve two message views: the original bytes used for randomization and the bytes visible after `R` has overwritten the aliased input for hashing."}}
