{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_155","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"find . -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%p\\\\n' | sort; sed -n '1,240p' CONFIGS.md; sed -n '1,180p' ERRORS.md; sed -n '1,180p' SYMBOLS.md\"","aggregated_output":"./.cargo/config.toml\n./CONFIGS.md\n./Cargo.lock\n./Cargo.toml\n./ERRORS.md\n./SYMBOLS.md\n./src/address.rs\n./src/api.rs\n./src/blake.rs\n./src/context.rs\n./src/ffi.rs\n./src/fips202.rs\n./src/fors.rs\n./src/haraka.rs\n./src/hash.rs\n./src/lib.rs\n./src/merkle.rs\n./src/offsets.rs\n./src/params.rs\n./src/randombytes.rs\n./src/sha2.rs\n./src/sign.rs\n./src/thash.rs\n./src/transcript.rs\n./src/utils.rs\n./src/utilsx1.rs\n./src/wots.rs\n./src/wotsx1.rs\n./target/.rustc_info.json\n./target/CACHEDIR.TAG\n./tests/differential.rs\n# Configuration Surface\n\n## Build-Time Matrix\n\nThe CMake axes are `HASH_BACKEND={haraka,sha2,shake,blake}`,\n`THASH={robust,simple}`, and\n`SECPAR={128f,128s,192f,192s,256f,256s}`. Cargo features mirror those axes and\nenforce exactly one feature from each group. The full 48-combination matrix is:\n\n| # | Cargo feature combination | `cargo check` |\n|---|---------------------------|---------------|\n| B01 | `haraka,robust,128f` | [x] |\n| B02 | `haraka,robust,128s` | [x] |\n| B03 | `haraka,robust,192f` | [x] |\n| B04 | `haraka,robust,192s` | [x] |\n| B05 | `haraka,robust,256f` | [x] |\n| B06 | `haraka,robust,256s` | [x] |\n| B07 | `haraka,simple,128f` | [x] |\n| B08 | `haraka,simple,128s` | [x] |\n| B09 | `haraka,simple,192f` | [x] |\n| B10 | `haraka,simple,192s` | [x] |\n| B11 | `haraka,simple,256f` | [x] |\n| B12 | `haraka,simple,256s` | [x] |\n| B13 | `sha2,robust,128f` | [x] |\n| B14 | `sha2,robust,128s` | [x] |\n| B15 | `sha2,robust,192f` | [x] |\n| B16 | `sha2,robust,192s` | [x] |\n| B17 | `sha2,robust,256f` | [x] |\n| B18 | `sha2,robust,256s` | [x] |\n| B19 | `sha2,simple,128f` | [x] |\n| B20 | `sha2,simple,128s` | [x] |\n| B21 | `sha2,simple,192f` | [x] |\n| B22 | `sha2,simple,192s` | [x] |\n| B23 | `sha2,simple,256f` | [x] |\n| B24 | `sha2,simple,256s` | [x] |\n| B25 | `shake,robust,128f` | [x] |\n| B26 | `shake,robust,128s` | [x] |\n| B27 | `shake,robust,192f` | [x] |\n| B28 | `shake,robust,192s` | [x] |\n| B29 | `shake,robust,256f` | [x] |\n| B30 | `shake,robust,256s` | [x] |\n| B31 | `shake,simple,128f` | [x] |\n| B32 | `shake,simple,128s` | [x] |\n| B33 | `shake,simple,192f` | [x] |\n| B34 | `shake,simple,192s` | [x] |\n| B35 | `shake,simple,256f` | [x] |\n| B36 | `shake,simple,256s` | [x] |\n| B37 | `blake,robust,128f` | [x] |\n| B38 | `blake,robust,128s` | [x] |\n| B39 | `blake,robust,192f` | [x] |\n| B40 | `blake,robust,192s` | [x] |\n| B41 | `blake,robust,256f` | [x] |\n| B42 | `blake,robust,256s` | [x] |\n| B43 | `blake,simple,128f` | [x] |\n| B44 | `blake,simple,128s` | [x] |\n| B45 | `blake,simple,192f` | [x] |\n| B46 | `blake,simple,192s` | [x] |\n| B47 | `blake,simple,256f` | [x] |\n| B48 | `blake,simple,256s` | [x] |\n\nThe parameter shapes mechanically selected by the six `params-*.h` families\nare:\n\n| SECPAR | N | full height | D | subtree height | FORS height | FORS trees |\n|--------|---|-------------|---|----------------|-------------|------------|\n| 128f | 16 | 66 | 22 | 3 | 6 | 33 |\n| 128s | 16 | 63 | 7 | 9 | 12 | 14 |\n| 192f | 24 | 66 | 22 | 3 | 8 | 33 |\n| 192s | 24 | 63 | 7 | 9 | 14 | 17 |\n| 256f | 32 | 68 | 17 | 4 | 9 | 35 |\n| 256s | 32 | 64 | 8 | 8 | 14 | 22 |\n\n## Runtime Matrix\n\nEvery applicable row is repeated under all build combinations above. Length\nsets include the exact branch boundaries found in the C loops and padding\ncode. Random-data rows use a fixed-seed generator and multiple samples.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-|\n| C01 | `crypto_sign_secretkeybytes`, `crypto_sign_publickeybytes`, `crypto_sign_bytes`, `crypto_sign_seedbytes` | all parameter sets; compare all size constants | [ ] |\n| C02 | `SPX_ull_to_bytes` | output lengths 0, 1, 4, 8, and 12; random `u64` | [ ] |\n| C03 | `SPX_u32_to_bytes` | random `u32`, including 0 and `UINT32_MAX` | [ ] |\n| C04 | `SPX_bytes_to_ull` | input lengths 0 through 8; random bytes | [ ] |\n| C05 | `SPX_set_layer_addr` | random address and values whose high bytes truncate | [ ] |\n| C06 | `SPX_set_tree_addr` | random address; 0, random, and `UINT64_MAX` | [ ] |\n| C07 | `SPX_set_type` | all seven documented types and out-of-range `u32` truncation | [ ] |\n| C08 | `SPX_set_keypair_addr` | random address and full `u32` range | [ ] |\n| C09 | `SPX_set_chain_addr` | random address and high-byte truncation | [ ] |\n| C10 | `SPX_set_hash_addr` | random address and high-byte truncation | [ ] |\n| C11 | `SPX_set_tree_height` | random address and high-byte truncation | [ ] |\n| C12 | `SPX_set_tree_index` | random address and full `u32` range | [ ] |\n| C13 | `SPX_copy_subtree_addr` | random source/destination, backend-specific address offsets | [ ] |\n| C14 | `SPX_copy_keypair_addr` | random source/destination, backend-specific address offsets | [ ] |\n| C15 | `SPX_initialize_hash_function` | random public/secret seeds; no-op, seeded SHA state, or tweaked Haraka constants | [ ] |\n| C16 | `SPX_prf_addr` | initialized context and random addresses | [ ] |\n| C17 | `SPX_gen_message_random` | messages of length 0, 1, block-boundary-1, block-boundary, block-boundary+1, and long | [ ] |\n| C18 | `SPX_hash_message` | messages crossing each backend's short/long branch; compare digest, tree, and leaf index | [ ] |\n| C19 | `SPX_thash` | `inblocks == 1` special case, robust and simple | [ ] |\n| C20 | `SPX_thash` | `inblocks == 2`, including wide-hash branch for N >= 24 | [ ] |\n| C21 | `SPX_thash` | `inblocks == SPX_WOTS_LEN` | [ ] |\n| C22 | `SPX_thash` | `inblocks == SPX_FORS_TREES` | [ ] |\n| C23 | `SPX_chain_lengths` | all-zero, all-`0xff`, and random N-byte messages | [ ] |\n| C24 | `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1` | requested leaf equals and differs from signing leaf | [ ] |\n| C25 | `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig` | random signatures/messages and initialized context | [ ] |\n| C26 | `SPX_compute_root` | even/odd leaf index; heights 1 and native subtree/FORS heights | [ ] |\n| C27 | `SPX_treehash` | deterministic callback; heights 1, 2, native subtree height; offset 0/nonzero | [ ] |\n| C28 | `SPX_wots_treehashx1` | valid leaf first/middle/last and offset 0/nonzero | [ ] |\n| C29 | `SPX_fors_gen_leafx1` | random initialized context/address and boundary indices | [ ] |\n| C30 | `SPX_fors_treehashx1` | valid leaf first/middle/last and per-tree offsets | [ ] |\n| C31 | `SPX_fors_sign`, `SPX_fors_pk_from_sig` | randomized messages/contexts/addresses; direct signing and reconstruction | [ ] |\n| C32 | `SPX_merkle_sign` | valid leaf first/middle/last in native subtree | [ ] |\n| C33 | `SPX_merkle_gen_root` | randomized initialized contexts | [ ] |\n| C34 | `crypto_sign_seed_keypair` | randomized seeds; compare complete public and secret keys | [ ] |\n| C35 | `crypto_sign_keypair` | deterministic RNG initialized identically before each call | [ ] |\n| C36 | `crypto_sign_signature` | deterministic RNG; empty, one-byte, boundary, and randomized messages | [ ] |\n| C37 | `crypto_sign_verify` | valid randomized detached signatures | [ ] |\n| C38 | `crypto_sign` | in-place/overlapping input and separate input; varied message lengths | [ ] |\n| C39 | `crypto_sign_open` | valid signed messages; output aliases and does not alias signed input | [ ] |\n| C40 | `AES256_ECB` | random keys and counter blocks | [ ] |\n| C41 | `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` | non-null random 48-byte provided data | [ ] |\n| C42 | `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` | null provided data | [ ] |\n| C43 | `randombytes_init`, `randombytes`, `DRBG_ctx` | null personalization; lengths 0, 1, 15, 16, 17, and multiple blocks | [ ] |\n| C44 | `randombytes_init`, `randombytes`, `DRBG_ctx` | non-null personalization; repeated calls and counter carry | [ ] |\n| C45 | `seedexpander_init` | max lengths 0, 1, block boundary, and `2^32-1`; random seed/diversifier | [ ] |\n| C46 | `seedexpander` | successful zero, partial-buffer, exact-block, cross-block, and repeated requests | [ ] |\n| C47 | `cst` | all 16 exported BLAKE constants | [ ] |\n| C48 | `blake256`, `blake512` | lengths 0, 1, padding boundary-1/boundary/+1, block boundary-1/boundary/+1, and multi-block | [ ] |\n| C49 | `blake256_init/update/final`, `blake512_init/update/final` | one-shot and split incremental updates at fill boundaries | [ ] |\n| C50 | `blake256_compress`, `blake512_compress` | initialized and randomized states with random full blocks | [ ] |\n| C51 | `SPX_blake256_mgf1`, `SPX_blake512_mgf1` | output lengths 0, 1, digest-1/digest/digest+1, and multiple digests | [ ] |\n| C52 | `sha256`, `sha512` | lengths crossing 56/64 and 112/128 padding/block boundaries | [ ] |\n| C53 | `sha256_inc_init/blocks/finalize`, `sha512_inc_init/blocks/finalize` | zero/one/multiple blocks plus both final-padding branches | [ ] |\n| C54 | `SPX_mgf1_256`, `SPX_mgf1_512` | output lengths 0, 1, digest-1/digest/digest+1, and multiple digests | [ ] |\n| C55 | `SPX_seed_state` | N = 16 versus N >= 24 context layouts | [ ] |\n| C56 | `shake256` | input/output lengths 0, 1, rate-1/rate/rate+1, and multi-rate | [ ] |\n| C57 | `shake256_absorb`, `shake256_squeezeblocks` | zero/one/multiple absorb and squeeze blocks | [ ] |\n| C58 | `shake256_inc_init/absorb/finalize/squeeze` | split absorbs and split squeezes crossing the 136-byte rate | [ ] |\n| C59 | `SPX_tweak_constants` | N = 16, 24, and 32 public seeds | [ ] |\n| C60 | `SPX_haraka_S` | input/output lengths 0, 1, rate-1/rate/rate+1 and output remainder | [ ] |\n| C61 | `SPX_haraka_S_inc_init/absorb/finalize/squeeze` | split absorbs/squeezes crossing the 32-byte rate | [ ] |\n| C62 | `SPX_haraka512_perm`, `SPX_haraka512`, `SPX_haraka256` | randomized full-width inputs and initialized contexts | [ ] |\n\n# Error Surface\n\nThis table is derived from rejection branches in the shared-library C sources.\nThe KAT driver is an executable, not part of the shared-library API, so its\ndriver-only exit codes are excluded. Compile-time `#error` directives reject\ninvalid builds rather than runtime inputs and are covered by the feature matrix.\nPointers not explicitly checked by C have undefined behavior and are not\ninvented here as C rejection cases.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|-|\n| 1 | `seedexpander_init` | `maxlen >= 0x100000000` | `RNG_BAD_MAXLEN` (`-1`) | [ ] |\n| 2 | `seedexpander` | `x == NULL` | `RNG_BAD_OUTBUF` (`-2`) | [ ] |\n| 3 | `seedexpander` | `xlen >= ctx->length_remaining` (including equality) | `RNG_BAD_REQ_LEN` (`-3`) | [ ] |\n| 4 | `crypto_sign_verify` | `siglen != SPX_BYTES` | `-1` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `crypto_sign_verify` | computed root differs from `pk + SPX_N` | `-1` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `crypto_sign_open` | `smlen < SPX_BYTES` | zero `m[0..smlen]`, set `*mlen = 0`, return `-1` | [ ] |\n| 7 | `crypto_sign_open` | embedded signature verification returns nonzero | zero `m[0..smlen]`, set `*mlen = 0`, return `-1` | [ ] |\n\n# Exported Symbol Surface\n\nGenerated from the union of `nm -D --defined-only` over the default C build:\n\n- `c_src/build/app/libsphincs_core.so`\n- `c_src/build/app/libsphincs_core_det.so`\n- `c_src/build/lib/blake/libblake.so`\n\n`T`, `B`, and `R` are the ELF symbol types reported by `nm`. Duplicate\ndefinitions shared by the two core libraries or by the backend are listed once.\n\n| # | C symbol | type | Rust export |\n|---|----------|------|-------------|\n| 1 | `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update` | T | [x] |\n| 2 | `AES256_ECB` | T | [x] |\n| 3 | `DRBG_ctx` | B | [x] |\n| 4 | `SPX_blake256_mgf1` | T | [x] |\n| 5 | `SPX_blake512_mgf1` | T | [x] |\n| 6 | `SPX_bytes_to_ull` | T | [x] |\n| 7 | `SPX_chain_lengths` | T | [x] |\n| 8 | `SPX_compute_root` | T | [x] |\n| 9 | `SPX_copy_keypair_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 10 | `SPX_copy_subtree_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 11 | `SPX_fors_gen_leafx1` | T | [x] |\n| 12 | `SPX_fors_pk_from_sig` | T | [x] |\n| 13 | `SPX_fors_sign` | T | [x] |\n| 14 | `SPX_fors_treehashx1` | T | [x] |\n| 15 | `SPX_gen_message_random` | T | [x] |\n| 16 | `SPX_hash_message` | T | [x] |\n| 17 | `SPX_initialize_hash_function` | T | [x] |\n| 18 | `SPX_merkle_gen_root` | T | [x] |\n| 19 | `SPX_merkle_sign` | T | [x] |\n| 20 | `SPX_prf_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 21 | `SPX_set_chain_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 22 | `SPX_set_hash_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 23 | `SPX_set_keypair_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 24 | `SPX_set_layer_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 25 | `SPX_set_tree_addr` | T | [x] |\n| 26 | `SPX_set_tree_height` | T | [x] |\n| 27 | `SPX_set_tree_index` | T | [x] |\n| 28 | `SPX_set_type` | T | [x] |\n| 29 | `SPX_thash` | T | [x] |\n| 30 | `SPX_treehash` | T | [x] |\n| 31 | `SPX_u32_to_bytes` | T | [x] |\n| 32 | `SPX_ull_to_bytes` | T | [x] |\n| 33 | `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1` | T | [x] |\n| 34 | `SPX_wots_pk_from_sig` | T | [x] |\n| 35 | `SPX_wots_treehashx1` | T | [x] |\n| 36 | `blake256` | T | [x] |\n| 37 | `blake256_compress` | T | [x] |\n| 38 | `blake256_final` | T | [x] |\n| 39 | `blake256_init` | T | [x] |\n| 40 | `blake256_update` | T | [x] |\n| 41 | `blake512` | T | [x] |\n| 42 | `blake512_compress` | T | [x] |\n| 43 | `blake512_final` | T | [x] |\n| 44 | `blake512_init` | T | [x] |\n| 45 | `blake512_update` | T | [x] |\n| 46 | `crypto_sign` | T | [x] |\n| 47 | `crypto_sign_bytes` | T | [x] |\n| 48 | `crypto_sign_keypair` | T | [x] |\n| 49 | `crypto_sign_open` | T | [x] |\n| 50 | `crypto_sign_publickeybytes` | T | [x] |\n| 51 | `crypto_sign_secretkeybytes` | T | [x] |\n| 52 | `crypto_sign_seed_keypair` | T | [x] |\n| 53 | `crypto_sign_seedbytes` | T | [x] |\n| 54 | `crypto_sign_signature` | T | [x] |\n| 55 | `crypto_sign_verify` | T | [x] |\n| 56 | `cst` | R | [x] |\n| 57 | `randombytes` | T | [x] |\n| 58 | `randombytes_init